## Residual opportunities after moving directives to a hash table

Done since these notes were first written: `dir_ifdef` / `dir_ifndef` share
`process_conditional_common` (a `COND_INVERT` flag flips the decision), there
are no `dir_*` JMP stubs any more, `process_directive` dispatches through
`JUMP_TARGET16` rather than borrowing `INST_PTR16`, the `MODE_END` value in
the `instgen.asm` header comment is correct ($0F), and the nesting limit has a
test (`17/tests/asm/13-conditionals_edge_cases.txt`, error 24). In `instgen.asm`,
`populate_instruction_hash_table` and `populate_directive_hash_table` share
`hash_add_from_table`, and in skip mode `process_conditional_directive` finds
the directive with the hash lookup and compares its handler address with
`dir_ifdef`/`dir_ifndef`/`dir_else`/`dir_endif`, instead of a chain of
`compare_token` calls.

Still open:
- [ ] Use a named constant for the conditional nesting limit (`directives.asm`
  compares against the literal 17; `ELSE_SEEN_ARRAY` in `asm.asm` is 16 bytes).
- IHASHTAB holds 69 entries in 128 slots (~54% load); adding many more
  directives or mnemonics would start to collide. Not actionable now.
